# Python bytecode — never publish compiled artifacts; the pitch is "read the source."
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Saved conversation transcripts from the /save command and the `wrap logs` verb,
# plus the per-turn metadata sidecar `wrap logs` keeps. These are private by nature —
# they must never be committed to a public repo.
chat_*.txt
chat_*.jsonl

# Internal staging notes — never part of the public repo. Listed here so even a
# `git add -A` cannot carry them along (the underscore prefix means nothing to git).
_PUSH_NOTES_FOR_RON.md
